# Glosses for the Inferno readings. Verse text is filled from inferno.txt.
DATA.append(canto(1, 'A dark wood, three beasts, and Virgil.',
    'Halfway through his life, Dante is lost in a dark wood. Three beasts block the hill, and the poet Virgil comes to guide him.',
    [Q(1, 'In the middle of the journey of our life, I came to myself in a dark wood, because the straight way was lost.',
        "Nel=in the | mezzo=middle@mezzo | del=of the | cammin=path | di=of | nostra=our | vita=life@vita",
        "mi=myself | ritrovai=I found again | per=in | una=a | selva=wood@selva | oscura=dark",
        "ché=for | la=the | diritta=straight | via=way@via | era=was | smarrita=lost"),
     Q(4, 'It is hard to say what that wood was. It was wild, harsh, and thick, and thinking of it brings the fear back.',
        "Ahi=ah | quanto=how | a=to | dir=say | qual=what | era=it was | è=is | cosa=a thing@cosa | dura=hard",
        "esta=this | selva=wood@selva | selvaggia=wild | e=and | aspra=rough | e=and | forte=thick@forte",
        "che=which | nel=in the | pensier=thought | rinova=renews | la=the | paura=fear@paura"),
     Q(79, 'Are you that Virgil, the spring that pours out so wide a river of speech? I answered him with an ashamed face.',
        "Or=now | se'=are you | tu=you | quel=that | Virgilio=Virgil@Virgilio | e=and | quella=that | fonte=spring@fonte",
        "che=who | spandi=pour | di=of | parlar=speech | sì=so | largo=broad@largo | fiume=a river@fiume",
        "rispuos'=I answered | io=I | lui=to him | con=with | vergognosa=ashamed | fronte=brow")]))

DATA.append(canto(2, 'Evening, and Beatrice sends Virgil.',
    'Night is coming on, and Dante is afraid to go. Beatrice has sent Virgil to him, and she tells Virgil why.',
    [Q(1, 'The day was leaving, and the dark air was taking the animals of the earth off their work, and I alone.',
        "Lo=the | giorno=day@giorno | se=itself | n'andava=was going | e=and | l'aere=the air | bruno=brown",
        "toglieva=was taking | li=the | animai=creatures | che=that | sono=are | in=on | terra=earth@terra",
        "da=from | le=their | fatiche=labors | loro=their | e=and | io=I | sol=alone | uno=one"),
     Q(70, 'I am Beatrice, who sends you. I come from the place I long to return to. Love moved me, and it makes me speak.',
        "I'=I | son=am | Beatrice=Beatrice | che=who | ti=you | faccio=make | andare=go",
        "vegno=I come | del=from the | loco=place | ove=where | tornar=to return | disio=I long",
        "amor=love | mi=me | mosse=moved | che=which | mi=me | fa=makes | parlare=speak")]))

DATA.append(canto(3, 'The gate of Hell, and Charon.',
    'Dante and Virgil reach the gate of Hell and read the words over it. Charon then ferries the souls across the river.',
    [Q(1, 'Through me the way goes to the city of sorrow, to eternal pain, and among the lost people.',
        "Per=through | me=me | si=one | va=goes | ne=into | la=the | città=city@città | dolente=grieving",
        "per=through | me=me | si=one | va=goes | ne=into | l'etterno=eternal | dolore=pain@dolore",
        "per=through | me=me | si=one | va=goes | tra=among | la=the | perduta=lost | gente=people@gente"),
     Q(4, 'Justice moved my high maker. Divine power made me, the highest wisdom, and the first love.',
        "Giustizia=Justice@giustizia | mosse=moved | il=the | mio=my | alto=high@alto | fattore=maker",
        "fecemi=made me | la=the | divina=divine | podestate=power",
        "la=the | somma=highest | sapïenza=wisdom | e=and | 'l=the | primo=first@primo | amore=love@amore"),
     Q(7, 'Before me nothing was made except eternal things, and I last forever. Leave all hope, you who enter.',
        "Dinanzi=before | a= | me=me | non=not | fuor=were | cose=things | create=created",
        "se non=except | etterne=eternal | e=and | io=I | etterno=eternal | duro=I endure",
        "Lasciate=leave | ogne=every | speranza=hope@speranza | voi=you | ch'intrate=who enter")]))

DATA.append(canto(4, 'Limbo, where the good live without hope.',
    'The first circle holds virtuous people who died before Christ. They are not tortured, but they have no hope, and Virgil is welcomed back among the poets.',
    [Q(40, 'For those faults, and for no other sin, we are lost, and hurt only in this: without hope we live in longing.',
        "Per=for | tai=such | difetti=faults | non=not | per=for | altro=any other | rio=wickedness@reo",
        "semo=we are | perduti=lost | e=and | sol=only | di=of | tanto=so much | offesi=hurt",
        "che=that | sanza=without | speme=hope | vivemo=we live | in=in | disio=longing@disio",
        note='This rio means wickedness, the same word as reo. It is not the stream.'),
     Q(79, 'A voice said: Honor the highest poet. His shade returns, the one that had gone away.',
        "Intanto=meanwhile | voce=a voice@voce | fu=was | per=by | me=me | udita=heard",
        "Onorate=honor | l'altissimo=the loftiest | poeta=poet@poeta",
        "l'ombra=his shade | sua=his | torna=returns | ch'era=which had | dipartita=departed")]))

DATA.append(canto(5, 'Francesca tells how love took her.',
    'In the second circle the lustful are blown forever by the wind. Francesca tells Dante how reading a book led her and Paolo into love.',
    [Q(100, 'Love, which quickly takes hold of a gentle heart, seized this man for my beautiful body, which was taken from me, and the way it happened still hurts me.',
        "Amor=Love | ch'al=which in the | cor=heart | gentil=gentle | ratto=at once | s'apprende=takes hold",
        "prese=seized | costui=this man | de=of | la=the | bella=beautiful | persona=body@persona",
        "che=which | mi=from me | fu=was | tolta=taken | e=and | 'l=the | modo=way | ancor=still | m'offende=offends me"),
     Q(103, 'Love, which excuses no one who is loved from loving back, seized me so hard for his beauty that it still has not let me go.',
        "Amor=Love | ch'a=which to | nullo=no | amato=loved person | amar=to love | perdona=grants pardon",
        "mi=me | prese=seized | del=for | costui=this man's | piacer=beauty | sì=so | forte=hard@forte",
        "che=that | come=as | vedi=you see | ancor=still | non=not | m'abbandona=abandons me"),
     Q(121, 'There is no greater pain than remembering a happy time in the middle of misery, and your teacher knows that.',
        "E=and | quella=she | a=to | me=me | Nessun=no | maggior=greater | dolore=pain@dolore",
        "che=than | ricordarsi=remembering | del=of the | tempo=time@tempo | felice=happy",
        "nella=in | miseria=misery@miseria | e=and | ciò=that | sa=knows | 'l= | tuo=your | dottore=teacher@dottore")]))

DATA.append(canto(6, 'Cerberus, and a prophecy about Florence.',
    'The gluttons lie under filthy rain, and the three-headed Cerberus barks over them. A Florentine, Ciacco, tells Dante what is coming for the city.',
    [Q(13, 'Cerberus, a cruel unnatural beast, barks doglike with three throats over the people buried there.',
        "Cerbero=Cerberus@cerbero | fiera=beast@fiera | crudele=cruel | e=and | diversa=monstrous",
        "con=with | tre=three | gole=throats | caninamente=like a dog | latra=barks",
        "sovra=over | la=the | gente=people@gente | che=who | quivi=there | è=is | sommersa=sunk"),
     Q(73, 'Two men are just, and no one listens to them. Pride, envy, and greed are the three sparks that have set hearts on fire.',
        "Giusti=the just | son=are | due=two | e=and | non=not | vi=there | sono=are they | intesi=heeded",
        "superbia=pride | invidia=envy | e=and | avarizia=greed@avarizia | sono=are",
        "le=the | tre=three | faville=sparks | c'hanno=which have | i=the | cuori=hearts@cuore | accesi=lit",
        note='Commentators debate who the two just men are. The poem does not name them.')]))

DATA.append(canto(7, 'Plutus shouts, and Virgil quiets him.',
    'A barking voice guards the misers and the spendthrifts, who roll weights at each other. Virgil tells Dante the creature cannot stop their descent.',
    [Q(1, 'Plutus began in a clucking voice. The cry is an untranslatable shout, not a sentence. The wise, noble man who knew everything is about to answer.',
        "Pape=(no meaning) | Satàn,=(no meaning) | pape=(no meaning) | Satàn=(no meaning) | aleppe!=(no meaning)",
        "cominciò=began | Pluto=Plutus | con=with | la=the | voce=voice@voce | chioccia=hoarse",
        "e=and | quel=that | savio=wise man | gentil=noble | che=who | tutto=all | seppe=knew",
        note='Pape Satàn aleppe is an untranslatable shout. Do not read it as a sentence.'),
     Q(4, 'To steady me he said: Do not let your fear hurt you. Whatever power that one has, he will not keep us from going down this rock.',
        "disse=he said | per=in order | confortarmi=to comfort me | Non=do not | ti=you | noccia=let it harm",
        "la= | tua=your | paura=fear@paura | ché=for | poder=power | ch'elli=which he | abbia=may have",
        "non=not | ci=from us | torrà=will take | lo=the | scender=going down | questa=this | roccia=rock@roccia")]))

DATA.append(canto(8, 'A muddy soul asks who Dante is.',
    'Crossing the swamp of the wrathful, Dante meets a soul caked in mud. It is Filippo Argenti, who says he is one who weeps.',
    [Q(31, 'While we were hurrying over the dead channel, someone full of mud rose before me and said: Who are you, coming before your time?',
        "Mentre=while | noi=we | corravam=were coursing | la=the | morta=dead | gora=ditch",
        "dinanzi=in front of | mi=me | si fece=appeared | un=one | pien=full | di=of | fango=mud",
        "e=and | disse=said | Chi=who | se'=are | tu=you | che=who | vieni=come | anzi ora=before your hour"),
     Q(34, 'I said: If I come, I do not stay. But who are you, made so filthy? He answered: See, I am one who weeps.',
        "E=and | io=I | a=to | lui=him | S'i'=if I | vegno=come | non=not | rimango=remain",
        "ma=but | tu=you | chi=who | se'=are | che=who | sì=so | se' fatto=have been made | brutto=ugly",
        "Rispuose=he answered | Vedi=see | che=that | son=I am | un=one | che=who | piango=weeps")]))

DATA.append(canto(9, 'A warning to the reader, then a crash of sound.',
    'The fallen angels refuse to open the city of Dis. Dante pauses to tell the reader to look under the strange verses, and a terrifying noise comes over the water.',
    [Q(61, 'O you who have healthy minds, look at the teaching hidden under the veil of the strange verses.',
        "O=O | voi=you | ch'avete=who have | li=the | 'ntelletti=intellects | sani=healthy",
        "mirate=look at | la=the | dottrina=teaching | che=which | s'asconde=hides itself",
        "sotto=under | 'l=the | velame=veil | de=of | li=the | versi=lines | strani=strange"),
     Q(64, 'And already, up over the muddy waves, came a crash of sound full of terror, which made both shores shake.',
        "E=and | già=already | venìa=was coming | su=up | per=over | le=the | torbide=muddy | onde=waves@onda",
        "un=a | fracasso=crash | d'un=of a | suon=sound | pien=full | di=of | spavento=terror",
        "per=by | cui=which | tremavano=were trembling | amendue=both | le=the | sponde=shores")]))

DATA.append(canto(10, 'Farinata recognizes a fellow Florentine.',
    'Among the burning tombs of the heretics, Farinata degli Uberti hears Tuscan speech and asks Dante to stop.',
    [Q(22, 'O Tuscan, who go alive through the city of fire speaking so honorably, please stop in this place.',
        "O=O | Tosco=Tuscan | che=who | per=through | la=the | città=city@città | del=of | foco=fire",
        "vivo=alive@vivo | ten vai=keep going | così=thus | parlando=speaking | onesto=honorably",
        "piacciati=may it please you | di=to | restare=stay | in=in | questo=this | loco=place"),
     Q(25, 'Your speech makes it plain that you come from that noble homeland which I perhaps harmed too much.',
        "La= | tua=your | loquela=speech | ti=you | fa=makes | manifesto=plain",
        "di=from | quella=that | nobil=noble | patrïa=homeland | natio=native",
        "a=to | la=the | qual=which | forse=perhaps | fui=I was | troppo=too | molesto=harmful")]))

DATA.append(canto(11, 'Why fraud is punished lower than violence.',
    'Virgil explains the plan of lower Hell. Violence and fraud are both injustice, but fraud is worse because it is a specially human evil.',
    [Q(22, 'Of every malice that earns hatred in Heaven, the end is injury, and every such end hurts someone, by force or by fraud.',
        "D'ogne=of every | malizia=malice | ch'odio=which hatred | in=in | cielo=Heaven@cielo | acquista=gains",
        "ingiuria=harm | è=is | 'l=the | fine=end | ed=and | ogne=every | fin=end | cotale=of that kind",
        "o=either | con=by | forza=force@forza | o=or | con=by | frode=fraud@frode | altrui=another | contrista=grieves"),
     Q(25, 'But because fraud is the evil that belongs to man, it displeases God more, so the fraudulent are lower, and more pain attacks them.',
        "Ma=but | perché=because | frode=fraud@frode | è=is | de=of | l'uom=man | proprio=own | male=evil@male",
        "più=more | spiace=it displeases | a= | Dio=God@dio | e=and | però=so | stan=they stand | di sotto=below",
        "li=the | frodolenti=fraudulent | e=and | più=more | dolor=pain | li=them | assale=assails")]))

DATA.append(canto(12, 'The river of blood, and a curse on greed.',
    'The violent against others boil in a river of blood, watched by centaurs. Virgil tells Dante to look down, and the poem turns on greed and rage.',
    [Q(46, 'Fix your eyes downhill, for the river of blood is coming near, where anyone who harmed another by violence boils.',
        "Ma=but | ficca=fix | li=the | occhi=eyes@occhio | a valle=downward | ché=for | s'approccia=draws near",
        "la=the | riviera=river | del=of | sangue=blood@sangue | in=in | la=the | qual=which | bolle=boils",
        "qual che=whoever | per=by | vïolenza=violence | in=against | altrui=another | noccia=does harm"),
     Q(49, 'O blind greed and mad anger, which spur us so in the short life, and then soak us so badly in the eternal one.',
        "Oh=O | cieca=blind | cupidigia=greed | e=and | ira=anger@ira | folle=mad",
        "che=which | sì=so | ci=us | sproni=you spur | ne=in | la=the | vita=life@vita | corta=short@corto",
        "e=and | ne=in | l'etterna=the eternal | poi=afterwards | sì=so | mal=badly@male | c'immolle=soaks us")]))

DATA.append(canto(13, 'Dante breaks a twig, and the tree speaks.',
    'The suicides are thorny trees. Dante snaps a twig, blood runs, and the trunk asks why he has no pity.',
    [Q(31, 'Then I put my hand out a little and picked a twig from a great thornbush, and its trunk cried: Why do you break me?',
        "Allor=then | porsi=I put | la=the | mano=hand@mano | un poco=a little | avante=forward",
        "e=and | colsi=I plucked | un=a | ramicel=small branch | da=from | un=a | gran=great | pruno=thorn",
        "e=and | 'l=the | tronco=trunk@tronco | suo=its | gridò=cried | Perché=why | mi=me | schiante=you splinter"),
     Q(34, 'Once it was dark with blood, it spoke again: Why do you tear me? Do you have no spirit of pity?',
        "Da=from | che=that | fatto=made | fu=it was | poi=then | di=with | sangue=blood@sangue | bruno=dark",
        "ricominciò=it began again | a dir=to say | Perché=why | mi=me | scerpi=you rip",
        "non=not | hai=have | tu=you | spirto=spirit | di=of | pietade=pity | alcuno=any")]))

DATA.append(canto(14, 'Capaneus still defies Jove.',
    'Blasphemers lie on burning sand under a rain of fire. Capaneus shouts that he is the same dead as he was alive, and he dares Jove to weary his smith.',
    [Q(49, 'The same man, noticing that I was asking my leader about him, shouted: As I was alive, so I am dead.',
        "E=and | quel=that | medesmo=same man | che=who | si=himself | fu=had | accorto=noticed",
        "ch'io=that I | domandava=was asking | il= | mio=my | duca=leader@duca | di=about | lui=him",
        "gridò=shouted | Qual=such as | io=I | fui=was | vivo=alive@vivo | tal=so | son=I am | morto=dead@morto"),
     Q(52, 'If Jove should wear out his smith, from whom in anger he took the sharp bolt that struck me on my last day, or wear out the others, shift after shift, at the black forge in Mongibello, crying “Good Vulcan, help, help!” as he did at the battle of Phlegra, and shoot me with all his strength, he could not have a glad revenge.',
        "Se=if | Giove=Jove@giove | stanchi=should weary | 'l=the | suo=his | fabbro=smith | da=from | cui=whom",
        "crucciato=angered | prese=he took | la=the | folgore=bolt | aguta=sharp",
        "onde=with which | l'ultimo=the last | dì=day | percosso=struck | fui=I was",
        "o=or | s'elli=if he | stanchi=should weary | li=the | altri=others | a=in | muta=a shift | a=after | muta=a shift",
        "in=in | Mongibello=Mongibello | a=at | la=the | focina=forge | negra=black",
        "chiamando=calling | Buon=good | Vulcano=Vulcan | aiuta=help | aiuta=help",
        "sì=just | com'=as | el=he | fece=did | a=at | la=the | pugna=battle | di=of | Flegra=Phlegra",
        "e=and | me=me | saetti=should shoot | con=with | tutta=all | sua=his | forza=strength@forza",
        "non=not | ne=from it | potrebbe=could | aver=have | vendetta=revenge@vendetta | allegra=glad")]))

DATA.append(canto(15, 'Dante meets his old teacher, Brunetto.',
    'On the burning sand a scorched soul takes Dante by the hem. It is Brunetto Latini, who once taught him how a person makes a name that lasts.',
    [Q(22, 'Eyed that way by such a company, I was recognized by one who took me by the hem and cried: What a wonder!',
        "Così=so | adocchiato=looked at | da=by | cotal=such | famiglia=a company@famiglia",
        "fui=I was | conosciuto=recognized | da=by | un=one | che=who | mi=me | prese=took",
        "per=by | lo=the | lembo=hem | e=and | gridò=cried | Qual=what | maraviglia=a wonder"),
     Q(85, 'You used to teach me how a man makes himself eternal. How grateful I am, while I live, has to show in my speech.',
        "m'insegnavate=you taught me | come=how | l'uom=a man | s'etterna=eternalizes himself",
        "e=and | quant'=how much | io=I | l'abbia=hold it | in grado=as a favor | mentr'=while | io=I | vivo=I live",
        "convien=it is needful | che=that | ne=in | la= | mia=my | lingua=speech@lingua | si scerna=it be discerned")]))

DATA.append(canto(16, 'Dante unties a cord and gives it to Virgil.',
    'Three great Florentines ask after their city, and then Virgil asks for the cord Dante wears. Dante had once hoped to catch the spotted beast with it.',
    [Q(106, 'I had a cord girt around me, and with it I had once thought to catch the leopard by its painted hide.',
        "Io=I | avea=had | una=a | corda=cord@corda | intorno=around | cinta=girt",
        "e=and | con=with | essa=it | pensai=I thought | alcuna=one | volta=time@volta",
        "prender=to take | la=the | lonza=spotted beast | a=by | la=the | pelle=hide@pelle | dipinta=painted"),
     Q(109, 'After I had untied it completely, just as my leader had ordered, I handed it to him knotted and coiled.',
        "Poscia=after | ch'io=I | l'ebbi=had it | tutta=all | da me=from myself | sciolta=loosened",
        "sì come=just as | 'l=the | duca=leader@duca | m'avea=had | comandato=commanded me",
        "porsila=I offered it | a=to | lui=him | aggroppata=knotted | e=and | ravvolta=wound up")]))

DATA.append(canto(17, 'Geryon, the image of fraud, carries them down.',
    'The cord brings up Geryon, a beast with a pointed tail and an honest face. Virgil tells him to descend gently, because of the new weight on his back.',
    [Q(1, 'Behold the beast with the pointed tail, who passes mountains and breaks walls and armor. Behold the one who makes the whole world stink.',
        "Ecco=behold | la=the | fiera=beast@fiera | con=with | la=the | coda=tail@coda | aguzza=pointed",
        "che=who | passa=passes | i=the | monti=mountains@monte | e=and | rompe=breaks | i=the | muri=walls | e=and | l'armi=the weapons",
        "Ecco=behold | colei=her | che=who | tutto=the whole | 'l= | mondo=world@mondo | appuzza=makes stink"),
     Q(97, 'And he said: Geryon, move now. Let the circles be wide and the descent small. Think of the new load you have.',
        "e=and | disse=he said | Gerïon=Geryon | moviti=move yourself | omai=now",
        "le=the | rote=wheels | larghe=wide@largo | e=and | lo=the | scender=descent | sia=let it be | poco=small",
        "pensa=think of | la=the | nova=new | soma=burden | che=which | tu=you | hai=have")]))

DATA.append(canto(18, 'Malebolge, the evil ditches.',
    'The eighth circle is a field of stone called Malebolge, with ten ditches of fraud. A deep pit opens in the middle.',
    [Q(1, 'There is a place in Hell called Malebolge, all of iron-colored stone, like the circle of wall that surrounds it.',
        "Luogo=a place | è=there is | in=in | inferno=Hell@inferno | detto=called | Malebolge=Malebolge@malebolge",
        "tutto=all | di=of | pietra=stone@pietra | di=of | color=color | ferrigno=iron-dark",
        "come=like | la=the | cerchia=circuit | che=which | dintorno=around | il=it | volge=turns"),
     Q(4, 'In the exact middle of the evil field a very wide, deep well gapes, whose arrangement I will describe in its place.',
        "Nel=in the | dritto=straight | mezzo=middle@mezzo | del=of the | campo=field@campo | maligno=evil",
        "vaneggia=gapes | un=a | pozzo=well@pozzo | assai=very | largo=wide@largo | e=and | profondo=deep",
        "di=of | cui=which | suo=its | loco=place | dicerò=I shall tell | l'ordigno=the structure")]))

DATA.append(canto(19, 'The simonists, and a pope who expects Boniface.',
    'Those who sold holy things are stuck head-down in holes, with flames on their feet. Pope Nicholas III mistakes Dante for Boniface.',
    [Q(1, 'O Simon Magus, O wretched followers: the things of God, which ought to be brides of goodness, and you, greedy.',
        "O=O | Simon mago=Simon Magus | o=O | miseri=wretched | seguaci=followers",
        "che=who | le=the | cose=things | di=of | Dio=God@dio | che=which | di=to | bontate=goodness",
        "deon=ought | essere=to be | spose=brides | e=and | voi=you | rapaci=rapacious"),
     Q(4, 'For gold and silver you make them adulterous. Now the trumpet must sound for you, since you are in the third ditch.',
        "per=for | oro=gold@oro | e=and | per=for | argento=silver@argento | avolterate=you prostitute",
        "or=now | convien=it must | che=that | per=for | voi=you | suoni=sound | la=the | tromba=trumpet@tromba",
        "però che=because | ne=in | la=the | terza=third | bolgia=pouch | state=you stand"),
     Q(52, 'And he shouted: Are you already standing there, are you already standing there, Boniface? The writing lied to me by several years.',
        "Ed=and | el=he | gridò=shouted | Se'=are | tu=you | già=already | costì=there | ritto=upright",
        "se'=are | tu=you | già=already | costì=there | ritto=upright | Bonifazio=Boniface",
        "Di=by | parecchi=several | anni=years@anno | mi=me | mentì=lied | lo=the | scritto=writing")]))

DATA.append(canto(20, 'Pity is dead here, Virgil says.',
    'The diviners walk with their faces turned backward, and their tears run down between their shoulders. Virgil tells Dante not to pity them.',
    [Q(28, 'Here pity lives when it is truly dead. Who is more wicked than the person who brings pity to God’s judgment?',
        "Qui=here | vive=lives | la=the | pietà=pity@pietà | quand'=when | è=it is | ben=well | morta=dead",
        "chi=who | è=is | più=more | scellerato=wicked | che=than | colui=he",
        "che=who | al=to the | giudicio=judgment | divin=divine | passion=pity | comporta=brings"),
     Q(31, 'Raise your head, raise it, and see the one at whom the earth opened before the Thebans’ eyes, so that they all cried: Where are you rushing?',
        "Drizza=straighten | la=the | testa=head@testa | drizza=straighten | e=and | vedi=see | a cui=at whom",
        "s'aperse=opened | a=before | li=the | occhi=eyes@occhio | d'i=of the | Teban=Thebans | la=the | terra=earth@terra",
        "per ch'=so that | ei=they | gridavan=were crying | tutti=all | Dove=where | rui=are you rushing")]))

DATA.append(canto(21, 'A devil announces a grafter from Lucca.',
    'Corrupt officials are sunk in boiling pitch, and winged devils hook them. One devil arrives with a soul from Lucca and jokes that everyone there takes bribes.',
    [Q(37, 'From our bridge he said: O Malebranche, here is one of the elders of Santa Zita. Put him under, for I am going back for more.',
        "Del=from | nostro=our | ponte=bridge@ponte | disse=he said | O=O | Malebranche=Malebranche@malebranche",
        "ecco=here | un=one | de=of | li=the | anzïan=elders | di=of | Santa Zita=Santa Zita",
        "Mettetel=put him | sotto=under | ch'i'=for I | torno=am returning | per anche=for more"),
     Q(40, 'To that city which is well supplied with them. Every man there is a grafter except Bonturo. There, for money, no becomes yes.',
        "a=to | quella=that | terra=city@terra | che=which | n'è=is of them | ben=well | fornita=furnished",
        "ogn'=every | uom=man | v'è=there is | barattier=grafter | fuor che=except | Bonturo=Bonturo",
        "del=from the | no=no | per=for | li=the | denar=money | vi=there | si fa=is made | ita=yes",
        note='Bonturo Dati was Lucca’s most famous grafter, so “except Bonturo” means not even him. ita is an old word for yes: for money, no becomes yes.')]))

DATA.append(canto(22, 'A sinner shows his back, like a dolphin.',
    'One of the barrators leaps out of the pitch the way a dolphin shows its back, then hides again faster than lightning.',
    [Q(19, 'As dolphins, when they signal the sailors with the arch of the back that they should try to save their ship,',
        "Come=as | i=the | dalfini=dolphins | quando=when | fanno=make | segno=a sign",
        "a'=to | marinar=sailors | con=with | l'arco=the bow | de=of | la=the | schiena=back",
        "che=that | s'argomentin=they should plan | di=to | campar=save | lor=their | legno=ship"),
     Q(22, 'so, sometimes, to lighten the punishment, one of the sinners showed his back and hid it quicker than a flash.',
        "talor=at times | così=so | ad=to | alleggiar=lighten | la=the | pena=punishment@pena",
        "mostrav'=showed | alcun=some | de'=of the | peccatori=sinners@peccatore | 'l=the | dosso=back",
        "e=and | nascondea=hid | in=in | men=less | che=than | non=not | balena=a flash")]))

DATA.append(canto(23, 'Hypocrites in lead cloaks, and Caiaphas.',
    'Dante and Virgil escape the devils and find the hypocrites walking in gilded lead robes. Caiaphas is pegged naked to the ground, for telling the Pharisees that one man should die for the people.',
    [Q(1, 'Silent, alone, with no companion, we walked one ahead and the other behind, as Franciscan friars go along a road.',
        "Taciti=silent | soli=alone | sanza=without | compagnia=company",
        "n'andavam=we walked | l'un=the one | dinanzi=ahead | e=and | l'altro=the other | dopo=after",
        "come=as | frati=friars@frate | minor=Minor | vanno=go | per=along | via=a road@via"),
     Q(115, 'He said to me: That nailed man you are staring at counseled the Pharisees that it was fitting to put one man to torture for the people.',
        "mi=to me | disse=said | Quel=that | confitto=fixed man | che=whom | tu=you | miri=stare at",
        "consigliò=counseled | i=the | Farisei=Pharisees | che=that | convenia=it was fitting",
        "porre=to put | un=one | uom=man | per=for | lo=the | popolo=people@popolo | a'=to | martìri=torments")]))

DATA.append(canto(24, 'Vanni Fucci admits a theft from the sacristy.',
    'Thieves are hunted by snakes, and their bodies burn to ash and reform. Vanni Fucci says it hurts more to be seen here than it did to die, and he confesses a church theft.',
    [Q(133, 'Then he said: It grieves me more that you have caught me in the misery where you see me than when I was taken from the other life.',
        "poi=then | disse=he said | Più=more | mi=me | duol=it grieves | che=that | tu=you | m'hai colto=have caught me",
        "ne=in | la=the | miseria=misery@miseria | dove=where | tu=you | mi=me | vedi=see",
        "che=than | quando=when | fui=I was | de=from | l'altra=the other | vita=life@vita | tolto=taken"),
     Q(136, 'I cannot deny what you ask. I am put this far down because I was a thief at the sacristy of the fine vestments.',
        "Io=I | non=not | posso=can | negar=deny | quel che=what | tu=you | chiedi=ask",
        "in giù=down | son=I am | messo=placed | tanto=so far | perch'=because | io=I | fui=was",
        "ladro=a thief@ladro | a=at | la=the | sagrestia=sacristy | d'i=of the | belli=beautiful | arredi=furnishings")]))

DATA.append(canto(25, 'The thieves’ changes outdo Lucan and Ovid.',
    'A thief and a serpent trade shapes in front of Dante. He tells Lucan and Ovid to fall silent, because their transformations are less than this.',
    [Q(94, 'Let Lucan now be silent where he tells of wretched Sabellus and Nasidius, and wait to hear what is released now.',
        "Taccia=let him be silent | Lucano=Lucan | ormai=by now | là dov'=there where | e'=he | tocca=touches",
        "del=of | misero=wretched | Sabello=Sabellus | e=and | di=of | Nasidio=Nasidius",
        "e=and | attenda=let him attend | a=to | udir=hearing | quel=what | ch'or=that now | si scocca=is shot"),
     Q(97, 'Let Ovid be silent about Cadmus and Arethusa, for if in his poem he turns the man into a snake and the woman into a spring, I do not envy him.',
        "Taccia=let him be silent | di=about | Cadmo=Cadmus | e=and | d'Aretusa=Arethusa | Ovidio=Ovid",
        "ché=for | se=if | quello=the one | in=into | serpente=a serpent@serpente | e=and | quella=the other | in=into | fonte=a spring@fonte",
        "converte=he converts | poetando=while poetizing | io=I | non=not | lo=him | 'nvidio=envy")]))

DATA.append(canto(26, 'Ulysses tells his men to sail past the sun.',
    'False counselors burn inside flames. Ulysses tells how, near the end of life, he urged his small crew not to live like beasts but to follow virtue and knowledge.',
    [Q(112, 'O brothers, I said, who through a hundred thousand dangers have reached the west, to this so short watch',
        "O=O | frati=brothers@frate | dissi=I said | che=who | per=through | cento=a hundred | milia=thousand | perigli=perils",
        "siete=you have | giunti=arrived | a=at | l'occidente=the west",
        "a=to | questa=this | tanto=so | picciola=small | vigilia=vigil"),
     Q(115, 'of our senses that remains, do not refuse the experience, following the sun, of the world without people.',
        "d'i=of | nostri=our | sensi=senses@senso | ch'è=which is | del=of the | rimanente=what remains",
        "non vogliate=do not wish | negar=to deny | l'esperïenza=the experience@esperienza",
        "di retro=behind | al=the | sol=sun@sole | del=of the | mondo=world@mondo | sanza=without | gente=people@gente"),
     Q(118, 'Consider your origin. You were not made to live as beasts do, but to follow virtue and knowledge.',
        "Considerate=consider | la= | vostra=your | semenza=seed",
        "fatti=made | non=not | foste=you were | a=to | viver=live | come=as | bruti=brutes",
        "ma=but | per=in order | seguir=to follow | virtute=virtue | e=and | canoscenza=knowledge")]))

DATA.append(canto(27, 'Guido speaks only because he thinks Dante cannot return.',
    'Another flame is Guido da Montefeltro. He says he would stay silent if he believed his listener could ever go back to the world.',
    [Q(61, 'If I believed that my answer were to a person who might ever return to the world, this flame would stand without shaking any more.',
        "S'i'=if I | credesse=believed | che=that | mia=my | risposta=reply | fosse=were",
        "a=to | persona=a person@persona | che=who | mai=ever | tornasse=might return | al=to the | mondo=world@mondo",
        "questa=this | fiamma=flame@fiamma | staria=would stay | sanza=without | più=further | scosse=shakings"),
     Q(64, 'But since never from this depth has anyone returned alive, if I hear the truth, I answer you without fear of infamy.',
        "ma=but | però=since | che=that | già=already | mai=ever | di=from | questo=this | fondo=depth@fondo",
        "non=not | tornò=returned | vivo=alive@vivo | alcun=anyone | s'i'=if I | odo=hear | il=the | vero=truth@vero",
        "sanza=without | tema=fear | d'infamia=of infamy@infamia | ti=you | rispondo=I answer")]))

DATA.append(canto(28, 'A headless body carries its head like a lantern.',
    'Sowers of discord are hacked apart as they walk. Bertran de Born carries his own head, because he split a father from his son, and he names this the contrapasso.',
    [Q(118, 'I truly saw it, and it still seems that I see it: a trunk without a head going along just as the others of that sad flock went.',
        "Io=I | vidi=saw | certo=certainly | e=and | ancor=still | par=it seems | ch'io=that I | 'l=it | veggia=see",
        "un=a | busto=torso | sanza=without | capo=a head@capo | andar=going | sì come=just as",
        "andavan=were going | li=the | altri=others | de=of | la=the | trista=sad | greggia=herd"),
     Q(121, 'And the severed head held itself by the hair, hanging from the hand like a lantern, and that head looked at us and said: Oh me.',
        "e=and | 'l=the | capo=head@capo | tronco=cut | tenea=was holding | per=by | le=the | chiome=hair@chioma",
        "pesol=hanging | con=in | mano=the hand@mano | a guisa=in the manner | di=of | lanterna=a lantern",
        "e=and | quel=it | mirava=was looking at | noi=us | e=and | dicea=said | Oh me=oh me"),
     Q(140, 'Divided, I carry my brain, alas, away from its source, which is in this stump. So the counterpenalty is observed in me.',
        "partito=divided | porto=I carry | il= | mio=my | cerebro=brain | lasso=alas",
        "dal=from | suo=its | principio=beginning | ch'è=which is | in=in | questo=this | troncone=stump",
        "Così=so | s'osserva=is observed | in=in | me=me | lo=the | contrapasso=counterpenalty")]))

DATA.append(canto(29, 'Virgil tells Dante to stop staring at the wounded.',
    'The falsifiers are punished with disease. Dante wants to keep looking at the wounds, and Virgil asks why his eyes stay down among the hacked shades.',
    [Q(1, 'So many people and such strange wounds had made my eyes so drunk that they longed to stay and weep.',
        "La=the | molta=great | gente=crowd@gente | e=and | le=the | diverse=strange | piaghe=wounds@piaga",
        "avean=had | le= | luci=eyes | mie=my | sì=so | inebrïate=drunk",
        "che=that | de=of | lo= | stare=staying | a=to | piangere=weep | eran=they were | vaghe=desirous"),
     Q(4, 'But Virgil said to me: Why do you keep staring? Why does your sight still rest down there among the sad, chopped shades?',
        "Ma=but | Virgilio=Virgil@Virgilio | mi=to me | disse=said | Che=what | pur=still | guate=are you gazing",
        "perché=why | la= | vista=sight | tua=your | pur=still | si soffolge=props itself",
        "là giù=down there | tra=among | l'ombre=the shades | triste=sad | smozzicate=chopped short")]))

DATA.append(canto(30, 'Master Adam, burning with thirst, remembers the streams.',
    'Counterfeiters and impostors tear at each other. Master Adam, swollen with dropsy, craves a drop of water and names the streams of his home hills.',
    [Q(61, 'To the misery of Master Adam. Alive I had plenty of what I wanted, and now, alas, I crave a little drop of water.',
        "a=to | la=the | miseria=misery@miseria | del=of | maestro=master@maestro | Adamo=Adam@Adamo",
        "io=I | ebbi=had | vivo=alive@vivo | assai=much | di=of | quel=that | ch'i'=which I | volli=wanted",
        "e=and | ora=now | lasso=alas | un=a | gocciol=droplet | d'acqua=of water@acqua | bramo=I crave"),
     Q(64, 'The little brooks that come down from the green hills of the Casentino into the Arno, making their channels cold and soft.',
        "Li=the | ruscelletti=rivulets | che=which | d'i=from the | verdi=green@verde | colli=hills",
        "del=of the | Casentin=Casentino | discendon=come down | giuso=down | in=into | Arno=the Arno",
        "faccendo=making | i= | lor=their | canali=channels | freddi=cold | e=and | molli=soft")]))

DATA.append(canto(31, 'A giant’s face, then a shout that is not Italian.',
    'Giants stand in the pit around the frozen center, visible from the waist up. Nimrod’s face looks as huge as the bronze pinecone at Saint Peter’s, and his mouth shouts nonsense.',
    [Q(58, 'His face seemed to me long and thick as the pinecone of Saint Peter’s in Rome, and his other bones were in proportion.',
        "La=the | faccia=face@faccia | sua=his | mi=to me | parea=seemed | lunga=long | e=and | grossa=huge",
        "come=as | la=the | pina=pinecone | di=of | San Pietro=Saint Peter@Pietro | a=at | Roma=Rome@Roma",
        "e=and | a=in | sua=his | proporzione=proportion | eran=were | l'altre=the other | ossa=bones@osso"),
     Q(67, 'The fierce mouth began to shout words that are not Italian and have no meaning. Sweeter psalms would not have suited it.',
        "Raphèl=(not Italian) | maì=(not Italian) | amècche=(not Italian) | zabì=(not Italian) | almi=(not Italian)",
        "cominciò=began | a=to | gridar=shout | la=the | fiera=fierce | bocca=mouth@bocca",
        "cui=for which | non=not | si=it | convenia=was fitting | più=more | dolci=sweeter | salmi=psalms",
        note='Nimrod’s shout is not Italian. It has no meaning.')]))

DATA.append(canto(32, 'Dante grabs a traitor by the hair.',
    'Traitors to kin and country are frozen in the ice. Dante seizes one by the hair, and the soul still refuses to say his name.',
    [Q(97, 'Then I took him by the scruff and said: You will have to name yourself, or not a hair up here will be left on you.',
        "Allor=then | lo=him | presi=I took | per=by | la=the | cuticagna=nape",
        "e=and | dissi=I said | El=it | converrà=will be needed | che=that | tu=you | ti=yourself | nomi=name",
        "o=or | che=that | capel=hair | qui sù=up here | non=not | ti=to you | rimagna=remain"),
     Q(100, 'Then he said to me: Even if you scalp me, I will not tell you who I am, nor show you, though you strike me a thousand times on the head.',
        "Ond'=whereupon | elli=he | a=to | me=me | Perché=though | tu=you | mi=me | dischiomi=scalp",
        "né=neither | ti=you | dirò=will I tell | ch'io sia=who I am | né=nor | mosterrolti=show you",
        "se=though | mille=a thousand | fiate=times | in=on | sul=the | capo=head@capo | mi=me | tomi=you strike")]))

DATA.append(canto(33, 'Ugolino tells of the tower and the hunger.',
    'Count Ugolino lifts his mouth from the skull he is gnawing and tells how he and his sons starved in a locked tower. At the end he says hunger could do more than grief.',
    [Q(1, 'That sinner raised his mouth from the fierce meal, wiping it on the hair of the head he had wrecked from behind.',
        "La=the | bocca=mouth@bocca | sollevò=lifted | dal=from the | fiero=fierce | pasto=meal",
        "quel=that | peccator=sinner@peccatore | forbendola=wiping it | a'=on | capelli=the hair",
        "del=of the | capo=head@capo | ch'elli=which he | avea=had | di retro=from behind | guasto=ruined"),
     Q(4, 'Then he began: You want me to renew a desperate grief that squeezes my heart even in the mere thinking, before I speak of it.',
        "Poi=then | cominciò=he began | Tu=you | vuo'=want | ch'io=that I | rinovelli=renew",
        "disperato=desperate | dolor=grief | che=which | 'l=the | cor=heart | mi=me | preme=presses",
        "già=already | pur=merely | pensando=in thinking | pria=before | ch'io=I | ne=of it | favelli=speak"),
     Q(73, 'Already blind, I went groping over each of them, and I called them for two days after they were dead. Then hunger could do more than grief.',
        "già=already | cieco=blind@cieco | a brancolar=groping | sovra=over | ciascuno=each",
        "e=and | due=two | dì=days | li=them | chiamai=I called | poi che=after | fur=they were | morti=dead",
        "Poscia=then | più=more | che=than | 'l=the | dolor=grief | poté=could | 'l=the | digiuno=fasting",
        note='The line can mean that hunger killed him, or that hunger drove him to eat the bodies. It does not say which.')]))

DATA.append(canto(34, 'Satan in the ice, then the stars.',
    'At the center of the earth Satan stands in the ice, chewing Judas, Brutus, and Cassius. Virgil climbs down his body, the poets pass the center, and they come out to see the stars.',
    [Q(1, 'The banners of the king of Hell move forward toward us. Look ahead, my master said, and see if you can make him out.',
        "Vexilla=banners | regis=of the king | prodeunt=advance | inferni=of Hell",
        "verso=toward | di noi=us | però=therefore | dinanzi=ahead | mira=look",
        "disse=said | 'l=the | maestro=master@maestro | mio=my | se=whether | tu=you | 'l=him | discerni=discern",
        note='The first line is Latin, the hymn Vexilla regis prodeunt, with inferni, “of Hell,” added. It is not Italian.'),
     Q(28, 'The emperor of the painful kingdom stood out of the ice from mid-chest. I am closer in size to a giant than the giants are to his arms. See now how huge the whole must be, to fit a part like that.',
        "Lo=the | 'mperador=emperor | del=of the | doloroso=painful | regno=realm",
        "da=from | mezzo=mid | 'l=the | petto=chest@petto | uscia=was coming out | fuor=out | de=of | la=the | ghiaccia=ice",
        "e=and | più=more | con=with | un=a | gigante=giant@gigante | io=I | mi=myself | convegno=compare",
        "che=than | i=the | giganti=giants@gigante | non=not | fan=do | con=with | le=the | sue=his | braccia=arms@braccio",
        "vedi=see | oggimai=now | quant'=how great | esser=to be | dee=must | quel=that | tutto=whole",
        "ch'a=which with | così=such | fatta=made | parte=a part | si=itself | confaccia=fits"),
     Q(136, 'We climbed up, he first and I second, until through a round opening I saw the beautiful things the heavens carry. From there we came out to see the stars again.',
        "salimmo=we climbed | sù=up | el=he | primo=first@primo | e=and | io=I | secondo=second",
        "tanto=so far | ch'i'=that I | vidi=saw | de=some of | le=the | cose=things | belle=beautiful@bello",
        "che=which | porta=carries | 'l=the | ciel=heaven@cielo | per=through | un=a | pertugio=opening | tondo=round",
        "E=and | quindi=thence | uscimmo=we went out | a=to | riveder=see again | le=the | stelle=stars@stella")]))
